/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:8:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index="1" source="eval" puzzle_id="71e489b6" lines="7-19">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:11:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:12:Highlight black defects in blue foreground by surrounding them with orange.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:13:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:14:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:15:- Blue (1) foreground on black (0) bg; small black holes or protrusions within blue regions; occasional thin blue spurs into black areas.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:16:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:17:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:18:- Thin blue pixels mostly surrounded by black are absorbed into the background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:19:- Small black components (≤3 cells) and leaf pixels of larger black components are "defects."
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:20:- Each defect gets an orange (7) 8-neighbor halo; the defect pixels themselves stay black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:21:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:22:Key insight: Only structural anomalies—tiny isolated patches and dangling endpoints—are marked, not bulk black regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:23:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:24:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:25:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:26:<reference_puzzle index="2" source="train" puzzle_id="689c358e" lines="72-88">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:27:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:28:Mark each arrow-like sprite's pointed frame endpoint with its color and the opposite endpoint black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:29:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:30:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:31:- The grid has a one-pixel solid rectangular frame around a dominant interior background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:32:- Inside the frame are monochrome six-pixel sprites shaped as asymmetric T arrows.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:33:- Each sprite has a length-4 bar and a length-3 crossbar one cell closer to the pointed end.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:34:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:35:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:36:- For each sprite, follow its bar axis from the shorter end to the frame.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:37:- Paint that frame endpoint with the sprite color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:38:- Paint the opposite endpoint on the same row or column black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:39:- Leave the interior background, sprites, and all other frame pixels unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:40:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:41:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:42:- The direction is encoded by the crossbar's off-center position: the nearer end is the pointing end.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:43:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:44:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:45:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:46:<reference_puzzle index="3" source="eval" puzzle_id="db0c5428" lines="32-51">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:47:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:48:Expand a 3x3 block motif into a 5x5 block motif around its missing center.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:49:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:50:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:51:- Teal background surrounds one 9x9 foreground motif.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:52:- The motif is a 3x3 array of 3x3 blocks; the middle block is empty teal.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:53:- Colored pixels immediately around the empty middle block encode the border
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:54:  of the missing center block.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:55:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:56:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:57:- Keep the original 9x9 motif in place.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:58:- Copy each of the eight surrounding 3x3 blocks to the opposite outer slot
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:59:  of the implied 5x5 block grid, without rotating it.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:60:- Fill the center block from the eight pixels around the hole; its center is
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:61:  the motif's majority foreground color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:62:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:63:Key insight: The visible 9x9 motif is the middle of a larger periodic
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:64:block-level pattern, and the empty center is reconstructed from its immediate
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:65:inner boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:66:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:67:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:68:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:69:<reference_puzzle index="4" source="train" puzzle_id="470c91de" lines="48-65">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:70:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:71:Move each teal-cornered filled rectangle one cell diagonally toward its teal corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:72:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:73:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:74:- Dominant background surrounds several filled rectangular colored objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:75:- Each object has exactly one teal control pixel replacing one corner cell of
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:76:  its rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:77:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:78:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:79:- Treat the teal pixel as the missing corner of its colored rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:80:- Erase each original rectangle footprint, including the teal pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:81:- Repaint the completed rectangle shifted one cell diagonally in the direction
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:82:  of that teal corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:83:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:84:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:85:- The control pixel's corner position gives both the missing cell to restore
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:86:  and the diagonal motion vector.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:87:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:88:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:89:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:90:<reference_puzzle index="5" source="eval" puzzle_id="195c6913" lines="37-52">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:91:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:92:Simulate particles along a path with alternating turn direction at collisions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:93:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:94:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:95:- Top-left: 2x2 monochrome blocks define a repeating color cycle (left-to-right).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:96:- Isolated single pixels of a cycle color: start markers adjacent to the path.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:97:- A 2x2 monochrome block of a distinct color: end marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:98:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:99:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:100:- Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:101:- On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:102:- Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:103:- If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:104:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:105:Key insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:106:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:107:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:108:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:109:<reference_puzzle index="6" source="train" puzzle_id="522fdd07" lines="8-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:110:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:111:Cycle each solid odd-sided square to the next smaller centered square, wrapping a single pixel to a 9x9 square.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:112:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:113:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:114:- The grid has one dominant background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:115:- Every foreground object is a separated 4-connected monochrome solid square.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:116:- Square side lengths are odd and belong to the cycle 1, 3, 5, 7, 9.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:117:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:118:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:119:- Clear the canvas to the background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:120:- Keep each square's color and center.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:121:- Replace side length n by n - 2 when n > 1; replace side length 1 by side length 9.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:122:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:123:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:124:- The visible operation is on square size, not color: side lengths cycle 1 -> 9 -> 7 -> 5 -> 3 -> 1.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:125:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:126:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:127:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:128:<reference_puzzle index="7" source="train" puzzle_id="b71a7747" lines="10-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:129:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:130:Extract the hidden two-color image by compacting the rows and columns of its complete mask.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:131:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:132:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:133:The grid contains one pair of colors whose pixels occupy every cell in the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:134:cross product of their active rows and active columns; all other colors form
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:135:the surrounding filler or separators.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:136:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:137:Find that unique color pair, keep exactly the rows and columns touched by
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:138:the pair, and return the induced subgrid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:139:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:140:The target image is not chosen by color id; it is the only two-color mask
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:141:whose occupied pixels form a full rectangular row/column product after
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:142:deleting unused rows and columns.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:143:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:144:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:145:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:146:<reference_puzzle index="8" source="eval" puzzle_id="8b9c3697" lines="9-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:147:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:148:Insert red components into interior sockets of large structures, leaving a black trail.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:149:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:150:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:151:- bg = most common. Large non-bg, non-red structures with interior cavities.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:152:- Red components outside structures.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:153:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:154:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:155:- Interior sockets: bg cells inside a structure's bbox, adjacent to structure pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:156:- For each structure, find the direction where rays from sockets hit a red component.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:157:- Slide that component into the socket; paint traversed cells black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:158:- Unmatched reds vanish.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:159:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:160:Key insight: Docking direction is inferred by ray-casting from interior sockets to the nearest red component.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:161:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:162:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:163:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:164:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="train" puzzle_id="cf5fd0ad" lines="10-22">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:165:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:166:Build a four-quadrant rotational tiling of the input square.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:167:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:168:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:169:- The input is a square grid treated as one complete sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:170:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:171:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:172:- Each output quadrant is a 2x2 repetition of a rotated copy of the whole input.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:173:- The quadrant rotations are upper-left 180 degrees, upper-right 90 degrees
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:174:  clockwise, lower-left 90 degrees counterclockwise, and lower-right unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:175:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:176:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:177:- The output is a 4x4 grid of original-size blocks, not a per-pixel scale-up.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:178:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:179:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:180:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:181:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="train" puzzle_id="d753a70b" lines="81-93">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:182:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:183:Red diamond outlines contract by one layer and gray diamond outlines expand by one layer while other objects stay fixed.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:184:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:185:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:186:- A 16x16 orange-background grid contains one-cell-thick Manhattan-diamond outlines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:187:- Red and gray outlines are the changing objects; other colored diamond outlines are static.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:188:- Some outlines may be clipped by the grid boundary, but their visible pixels still fit a clipped Manhattan-distance contour.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:189:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:190:- Clear all red and gray pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:191:- Red objects are redrawn with the same diamond center and radius minus one.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:192:- Gray objects are redrawn with radius plus one; an ambiguous edge-clipped growing arc continues away from the nearest perpendicular edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:193:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:194:- The task is not about moving whole objects: each changing object is a contour of a diamond, and the visible operation is one step of contour contraction or expansion.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:195:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:196:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:197:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:198:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="eval" puzzle_id="7b80bb43" lines="8-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:199:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:200:Remove diagonal staircase noise and complete broken straight lines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:201:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:202:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:203:- bg = background; one foreground color fg forming axis-aligned lines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:204:- Some fg pixels form 45° diagonal chains (8-connected but 4-disconnected from lines).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:205:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:206:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:207:- Delete all diagonal-only fg pixels (those with no orthogonal fg neighbor, only diagonal ones).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:208:- Fill short gaps in horizontal/vertical lines where a deleted diagonal was nearby.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:209:- Prune remaining diagonal-adjacent leaf pixels near former diagonal sites.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:210:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:211:Key insight: Diagonal pixels are hints marking where a straight line is broken; their span sets the maximum gap size to fill.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:212:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:213:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:214:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:215:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="train" puzzle_id="9f8de559" lines="19-37">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:216:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:217:Erase the first border pixel hit by extending the red marker away from its pink trail.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:218:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:219:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:220:- The dominant background surrounds a unique red marker and a four-pixel
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:221:  pink trail.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:222:- The pink pixels form one straight 8-connected ray starting next to the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:223:  red marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:224:- In the opposite direction from that trail, the red marker faces a
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:225:  non-background border or obstacle pixel beyond background cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:226:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:227:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:228:- Keep the whole grid fixed except for the first non-background pixel on
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:229:  the ray from the red marker away from the pink trail.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:230:- Recolor that one hit pixel to the background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:231:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:232:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:233:- The pink trail marks where the red marker came from, so the edit is found
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:234:  by ray-casting from the red marker in the opposite direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:235:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:236:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:237:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:238:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="train" puzzle_id="8dab14c2" lines="120-133">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:239:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:240:Complete each boundary tab or notch by adding the complementary feature on the opposite side of the foreground object.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:241:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:242:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:243:- The grid has exactly two colors: a dominant background and one foreground object.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:244:- The foreground object is a thick rectilinear shape with one-pixel tabs and notches on its boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:245:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:246:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:247:- A foreground tab is a one-neighbor boundary pixel; project through its full row or column span and remove the opposite edge pixel to make a matching notch.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:248:- A background notch is a one-pixel cut with three foreground 4-neighbors; project across the full row or column span and add a tab just outside the opposite edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:249:- Notches immediately beside a tab source are not independent sources, because that gap belongs to the tab's local boundary shape.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:250:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:251:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:252:- The changed pixels are not color-specific noise; they are paired jigsaw-like boundary features on opposite sides of the same thick row or column cross-section.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:253:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:254:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:255:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:256:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="eval" puzzle_id="38007db0" lines="9-22">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:257:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:258:Extract the unique cell from each lattice row into a single-column lattice.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:259:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:260:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:261:- Grid divided into equal square cells by uniform gridlines of color L.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:262:- Cell interiors filled with bg; each cell has an inner sprite pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:263:- Each row of cells has exactly one cell with a unique pattern; the rest are copies.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:264:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:265:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:266:- For each lattice row, find the cell whose inner pattern appears exactly once (the "odd one out").
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:267:- Construct a single-column lattice preserving the original row heights, containing only the unique cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:268:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:269:Key insight: The task is per-row "odd one out" — every cell in a row is identical except one oddball, which must be extracted.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:270:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:271:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:272:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:273:<reference_puzzle index="15" source="eval" puzzle_id="58490d8a" lines="9-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:274:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:275:Count colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:276:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:277:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:278:- A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:279:- Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:280:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:281:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:282:- For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:283:- Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:284:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:285:Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:286:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:287:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:288:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:289:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="train" puzzle_id="2a28add5" lines="8-22">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:290:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:291:Paint each pink control pixel as a teal horizontal bar whose reach equals the foreground counts on that row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:292:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:293:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:294:- The grid has a dominant background color and one or more pink control pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:295:- Each marker row has exactly one pink pixel; all other non-background pixels
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:296:  in that row are counters.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:297:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:298:- Start from an all-background output grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:299:- For each pink pixel, count non-background pixels strictly to its left and
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:300:  strictly to its right in the same row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:301:- Paint teal from c - left_count through c + right_count on that row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:302:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:303:- The foreground pixels are not copied; only their counts on each side of
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:304:  each pink marker encode the teal bar length.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:305:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:306:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:307:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:308:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="train" puzzle_id="cc9053aa" lines="59-72">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:309:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:310:Recolor the unique safe route between the two maroon endpoints from teal to maroon.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:311:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:312:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:313:- A black background contains a teal 4-connected track, exactly two maroon endpoint pixels, and one or more orange blocker pixels embedded near the track.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:314:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:315:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:316:- Treat each orange blocker and its 8-neighborhood as forbidden.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:317:- In the remaining teal/maroon track graph, there is exactly one simple
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:318:  4-connected path between the maroon endpoints.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:319:- Recolor teal pixels on that path to maroon; leave endpoints, blockers, and all other cells unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:320:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:321:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:322:- The orange pixels block nearby teal cells diagonally as well as orthogonally, which removes shorter decoy routes and makes the intended endpoint-to-endpoint path unique.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:323:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:324:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:325:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:326:<reference_puzzle index="18" source="train" puzzle_id="a644e277" lines="31-50">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:327:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:328:Extract the lattice subregion bounded by the four background-colored corner holes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:329:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:330:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:331:- A regular one-cell-thick lattice has one line color, one background color,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:332:  and sparse marker pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:333:- Exactly four lattice-line intersections are background-colored holes instead
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:334:  of line-color pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:335:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:336:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:337:- Find the unique non-background color that forms regular horizontal and
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:338:  vertical lattice lines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:339:- Use the four background-colored lattice intersections as the corners of one
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:340:  rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:341:- Return the inclusive crop between those corner rows and columns.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:342:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:343:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:344:- The crop is marked by the missing lattice intersections, not by the marker
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:345:  pixels inside the cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:346:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:347:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:348:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:349:<reference_puzzle index="19" source="train" puzzle_id="f1bcbc2c" lines="40-55">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:350:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:351:Paint the top-connected middle channel between two orange path components teal.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:352:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:353:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:354:- The background is black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:355:- One foreground color forms exactly two 4-connected one-pixel-wide path components.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:356:- Optional non-background control pixels may sit in the channel between the two paths.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:357:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:358:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:359:- Dilate each path component by one cell in the 8-neighborhood and intersect the two dilations; this gives the one-cell-wide middle channel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:360:- A control pixel in that channel is a blocker only when its 4-neighbors touch fewer than both path components; otherwise it is part of the channel and is repainted.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:361:- After removing blockers, paint the channel component connected to the top edge teal and keep all other pixels unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:362:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:363:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:364:- The desired pixels are not found by region filling; they are the geometric overlap of the two paths' one-cell halos, with weakly attached control pixels splitting the channel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:365:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:366:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:367:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:368:<reference_puzzle index="20" source="train" puzzle_id="abbfd121" lines="56-74">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:369:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:370:Recover the repeating background pattern hidden under the largest solid rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:371:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:372:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:373:- The grid is covered by a small row/column periodic pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:374:- Several non-pattern colors form solid rectangular foreground objects that
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:375:  overwrite the pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:376:- The requested output region is the largest of those solid rectangles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:377:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:378:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:379:- Find every 4-connected monochromatic object whose bounding box is a filled
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:380:  rectangle with both dimensions greater than one.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:381:- Treat those rectangles as masks, infer the smallest repeating tile that is
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:382:  consistent with all remaining visible pixels, and repaint the largest
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:383:  rectangle's coordinates with that tile.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:384:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:385:Key insight: The rectangle colors are occluders; the visible pixels outside
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:386:them are enough to reconstruct the original periodic background underneath.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:387:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:388:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:389:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:390:你的任务：
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:391:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:392:创新方式包括但不限于：
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:393:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:394:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:395:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程"。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:396:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:397:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:398:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:399:<new_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:400:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:401:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:402:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:403:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:404:</new_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/15/prompt.md:405:
